ld be 16 minus 3, which is 13. \n\nSo, the answer should be 13 ceilings left to paint. Let me check again to make sure. \n\nTotal ceilings: 28. Painted this week: 12. Left: 28 - 12 = 16. Painted next week: 1/4 of 12 = 3. So remaining after next week: 16 - 3 = 13. \n\nYes, that seems right. Maybe I can verify with another method. Let me think. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can model this step by step. \n\nWeek 1: Painted 12 ceilings. Left: 28 - 12 = 16. \n\nWeek 2: Painted 1/4 of the current number. The current number here is 16, since that's what he has left. So 16 divided by 4 is 4. Wait, hold on! There's a confusion here. Wait, the problem says he paints 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week. This week he painted 12, so he paints 3 (12/4). Then the next week, he paints 1/4 of what he did this week, which is 12, so he paints 3? Or is it 1/4 of the current remaining after this week?\n\nWait, the problem says: next week, he will paint 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week. So does that mean 1/4 of that 12? Which is 3? Or does it mean 1/4 of the current number of ceilings, which is 28? Which is 7?\n\nHmm, this is a critical point. The wording says: \"Next week, he will paint 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week.\" This week, he did 12, so he paints 12 divided by 4, which is 3. So next week he paints 3. \n\nAlternatively, if it had said \"next week, he will paint 1/4 of the number of ceilings he has to paint,\" which is 28, then he would paint 7. But the problem says \"the number of ceilings he did this week.\" So he paints 1/4 of his 12. \n\nTherefore, the correct calculation is 12 divided by 4, which is 3. Then subtract that from the remaining 16. \n\nSo 16 - 3 = 13. \n\nAlternatively, maybe there's some confusion about \"included\" or \"excluding.\" Let me check once more. \n\nTotal ceilings: 28. This week: 12. So after this, 16 remaining. \n\nNext week, he paints 1/4 the number he did this week, which is 1/4 * 12 = 3. Therefore, subtract 3 from 16. \n\nYes, 16 - 3 = 13. \n\nTherefore, the answer is 13. \n\nI think that's correct. I don't see where I might have messed up. Let me recap:\n\nOriginal problem:\n\nMichelangelo has 28 ceilings.\n\nWeek 1: paints 12 of them. Left: 28 - 12 = 16.\n\nWeek 2: paints 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week (which is 12). So 12 divided by 4 is 3. Therefore, left after week 2: 16 - 3 = 13.\n\nAlternatively, someone might think that since he painted this week, maybe the 1/4 is of the total skyscrapers, but the problem says \"the number of ceilings he did this week,\" not the total, so the 1/4 is definitely 12. \n\nTherefore, the answer is 13. \n\n**Final Answer**\nThe number of ceilings left to paint is \\boxed{13}.\n</think>\n\nTo determine how many ceilings will be left to paint after Michelangelo finishes the week, we need to follow the given sequence of events:\n\n1. Michelangelo has a total of 28 ceilings to paint.\n2. This week, he paints 12 ceilings.  \n   Remaining ceilings after this week:  \n   $ 28 - 12 = 16 $.\n\n3. Next week, he will paint $ \\frac{1}{4} $ of the number of ceilings he painted this week.  \n   Since this week he painted 12, the number of ceilings he paints next week is:  \n   $ \\frac{12}{4} = 3 $.\n\n4. After painting 3 ceilings next week, the remaining number of ceilings to paint is:  \n   $ 16 - 3 = 13 $.\n\n---\n\n**Final Answer**:  \nThe number of ceilings left to paint is $\\boxed{13}$.<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Michelangelo has 28 ceilings to paint. This week, he paints 12 of them. Next week, he will paint 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week. How many ceilings will be left to paint after next week?", "answer": "After this week, Michelangelo will have 28-12=<<28-12=16>>16 more ceilings to paint.\nNext week, Michelangelo will paint 12/4=<<12/4=3>>3 ceilings.\nMichelangelo will have 16-3=<<16-3=13>>13 more ceilings to paint.\n#### 13", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Michelangelo has 28 ceilings to paint. This week, he paints 12 of them. Next week, he will paint 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week. How many ceilings will be left to paint after next week?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["13"], "solution": "13"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 44406, 87910, 702, 220, 17, 23, 55714, 311, 6177, 13, 1096, 2003, 11, 566, 56848, 220, 16, 17, 315, 1105, 13, 9295, 2003, 11, 566, 686, 6177, 220, 16, 14, 19, 279, 1372, 315, 55714, 566, 1521], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 752, 1430, 311, 7071, 700, 419, 3491, 3019, 553, 3019, 13, 2055, 11, 44406, 87910, 702, 220, 17, 23, 55714, 311, 6177, 13, 1096, 2003, 11, 566, 56848, 220, 16, 17, 315, 1105, 13, 5005, 11, 279, 1790, 2003, 11, 566, 56848, 220, 16, 14, 19, 279, 1372, 315, 55714, 566, 23983, 419, 2003, 13, 576, 3405, 374, 10161]}
