2026-10-30 07:59:46 INFO areno.api.trainers.policy_only.PolicyOnlyTrainer policy_only.py:723 - rollout_completion={"kind": "rollout", "epoch": 0, "step": 26, "prompt_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: John buys 1000 balloons.  Each balloon holds 10 liters of air.  If he buys 500-liter tanks of gas, how many tanks does he need to buy to fill all the balloons?\nSolution:", "decoded_prompt": "<|im_start|>user\nSolve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: John buys 1000 balloons.  Each balloon holds 10 liters of air.  If he buys 500-liter tanks of gas, how many tanks does he need to buy to fill all the balloons?\nSolution:<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n", "completion": "<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out this problem. So, John buys 1000 balloons. Each balloon holds 10 liters of air. If he buys 500-liter tanks, how many tanks does he need to buy to fill all the balloons?\n\nHmm. Let me break this down step by step. First, I need to find out how much air is needed to fill all the balloons. Then, since each tank is 500 liters, I should divide that by the total amount needed to find out how many tanks he needs. \n\nLet me start with the balloons. Each balloon is 10 liters. If he has 1000 balloons, then the total amount of air required is just 10 liters multiplied by the number of balloons. So that would be 10 times 1000. Let me calculate that. 10 * 1000 is 10,000 liters. Okay, so there's 10,000 liters of air needed.\n\nNow, each tank is 500 liters. So, to get the number of tanks, I divide the total amount needed by the capacity of one tank. So that's 10,000 liters divided by 500 liters per tank. Let me do the division. 10,000 divided by 500... Hmm, 500 times 20 is 10,000, right? Because 500 * 20 = 10,000. So that would mean 20 tanks. \n\nWait, let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes. If each balloon is 10 liters, 1000 balloons would be 10 * 1000 = 10,000 liters. Divided by a tank that's 500 liters gives 20. Yeah, that seems right. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I could think of it as 1000 balloons multiplied by 10 liters each divided by 500. So (1000 * 10)/500 = 10,000 / 500 = 20. Yep, same answer. \n\nI don't think I messed up here. The total volume is straightforward, and dividing by the tank's capacity gives the number of tanks needed. So the answer should be 20 tanks.\n\n**Final Answer**\nJohn needs to buy \\boxed{20} tanks of gas.\n</think>\n\nTo determine how many 500-liter tanks John needs to buy to fill 1000 balloons, each of which holds 10 liters of air, we start by calculating the total amount of air required to fill all the balloons.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Calculate the total volume of air needed\n\nEach balloon holds **10 liters**, and there are **1,000 balloons**, so:\n\n$$\n\\text{Total air needed} = 10 \\, \\text{liters/balloon} \\times 1,000 \\, \\text{balloons} = 10,000 \\, \\text{liters}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Determine how many 500-liter tanks are needed\n\nEach tank is **500 liters**, so to fill the 10,000 liters:\n\n$$\n\\frac{10,000 \\, \\text{liters}}{500 \\, \\text{liters/tank}} = 20 \\, \\text{tanks}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer\n\n$$\n\\boxed{20}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "John buys 1000 balloons.  Each balloon holds 10 liters of air.  If he buys 500-liter tanks of gas, how many tanks does he need to buy to fill all the balloons?", "answer": "He needs 1000*10=<<1000*10=10000>>10000 liters of gas\nSo he needs 10000/500=<<10000/500=20>>20 tanks\n#### 20", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: John buys 1000 balloons.  Each balloon holds 10 liters of air.  If he buys 500-liter tanks of gas, how many tanks does he need to buy to fill all the balloons?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["20"], "solution": "20"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 3757, 49531, 220, 16, 15, 15, 15, 69480, 13, 220, 8886, 46756, 9982, 220, 16, 15, 92866, 315, 3720, 13, 220, 1416, 566, 49531, 220, 20, 15, 15, 85594, 25866, 315, 6819, 11, 1246, 1657, 25866, 1558], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 752, 1430, 311, 7071, 700, 419, 3491, 13, 2055, 11, 3757, 49531, 220, 16, 15, 15, 15, 69480, 13, 8886, 46756, 9982, 220, 16, 15, 92866, 315, 3720, 13, 1416, 566, 49531, 220, 20, 15, 15, 85594, 25866, 11, 1246, 1657, 25866, 1558, 566, 1184, 311, 3695, 311, 5155, 678, 279, 69480, 1939, 80022, 13, 6771, 752, 1438, 419]}
