f the 4 matches in the last round.\" So \"half of the 4 matches\"—so that would mean half of 4, which is 2 matches. So he won 2 matches in the last round. \n\nSo putting it all together: first two rounds: 6 matches each, so 6 + 6 = 12 matches. Last round: half of 4, which is 2 matches. Therefore, total matches would be 12 + 2 = 14. Let me just make sure I didn't misunderstand something. The problem says \"He wins all of the matches in the first 2 rounds, each of which had 6 matches, then wins half of the 4 matches in the last round.\"\n\nYes, so yeah, first two rounds each with 6, so 12, then last round half of 4 is 2. Adding them gives 14. So the answer should be 14. Let me verify once more. First rounds: 2*6=12. Last round: 4/2=2. Total 14. Yep. Okay, that makes sense.\n\n**Final Answer**\nBrendan won \\boxed{14} matches throughout the competition.\n</think>\n\nTo determine how many matches Brendan won in total, we need to break down his wins into distinct parts of the competition.\n\n---\n\n### **Part 1: First 2 Rounds**\n\nEach of the three rounds (the first two rounds) included 6 matches. Since he won all of them, the total matches won for the first two rounds is:\n\n$$\n6 \\text{ matches} \\times 2 = 12 \\text{ matches}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **Part 2: Last Round**\n\nThe problem states that Brendan only wins half of the 4 matches in the last round. Therefore, the number of matches he won in the last round is:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{2} = 2 \\text{ matches}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **Total Matches Won**\n\nAdding both parts together:\n\n$$\n12 \\text{ matches (first two rounds)} + 2 \\text{ matches (last round)} = 14 \\text{ matches}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **Final Answer**\n\n$$\n\\boxed{14}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Brendan has entered a kickboxing competition and wins matches against multiple contestants. He wins all of the matches in the first 2 rounds, each of which had 6 matches, then wins half of the 4 matches in the last round. How many matches did Brendan win throughout the competition?", "answer": "In the first 2 rounds, Brendan wins a total of 2 rounds * 6 matches per round = <<2*6=12>>12 matches.\nIn the last round, Brendan wins half of the matches which is 4 matches / 2 = <<4/2=2>>2 matches.\nThroughout the competition, Brendan has therefore won 12 + 2 = <<12+2=14>>14 matches.\n#### 14", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Brendan has entered a kickboxing competition and wins matches against multiple contestants. He wins all of the matches in the first 2 rounds, each of which had 6 matches, then wins half of the 4 matches in the last round. How many matches did Brendan win throughout the competition?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["14"], "solution": "14"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 55843, 702, 10636, 264, 10323, 89174, 10707, 323, 14816, 9071, 2348, 5248, 74424, 13, 1260, 14816, 678, 315, 279, 9071, 304, 279, 1156, 220, 17, 19531, 11, 1817, 315, 892, 1030, 220, 21, 9071, 11, 1221, 14816], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 752, 1430, 311, 7071, 700, 1246, 1657, 9071, 55843, 2765, 304, 2790, 13, 576, 3491, 2727, 566, 14816, 678, 9071, 304, 279, 1156, 1378, 19531, 11, 1817, 448, 220, 21, 9071, 11, 1221, 566, 14816, 4279, 315, 279, 220, 19, 9071, 304, 279, 1537, 4778, 13, 88190, 11, 1077, 594, 1438, 419, 1495, 3019, 553, 3019, 382, 5338, 11]}
