 the dolls, she can only spend $3, so the remainder is $100 - 3 = $97. I don't think there's any hidden detail or trick here. The problem seems straightforward.\n\nSo, I think the answer is $97.\n</think>\n\nAmy’s grandfather gave her $100, and the cost of buying 3 dolls at $1 each is calculated as:\n\n$$\n3 \\times 1 = 3\n$$\n\nAmy then has:\n\n$$\n100 - 3 = 97\n$$\n\nThus, the final amount of money Amy has left is:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{97}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Amy's grandfather gave her $100 for her birthday. Amy bought 3 dolls, each of which cost $1. How much money does Amy have left?", "answer": "The cost of the dolls is 3 × $1 = $<<3*1=3>>3.\nAmy has $100 − $3 = $97 left.\n#### 97", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Amy's grandfather gave her $100 for her birthday. Amy bought 3 dolls, each of which cost $1. How much money does Amy have left?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["97"], "solution": "97"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 28693, 594, 37850, 6551, 1059, 400, 16, 15, 15, 369, 1059, 15198, 13, 28693, 10788, 220, 18, 63781, 11, 1817, 315, 892, 2783, 400, 16, 13, 2585, 1753, 3220, 1558, 28693, 614, 2115, 5267, 36842, 25, 151645], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 752, 1430, 311, 7071, 700, 1246, 1753, 3220, 28693, 702, 2115, 13, 2055, 11, 28693, 594, 37850, 6551, 1059, 400, 16, 15, 15, 369, 1059, 15198, 13, 5005, 1340, 10788, 220, 18, 63781, 11, 323, 1817, 7649, 7049, 400, 16, 13, 88190, 11, 1077, 594, 1438, 419, 1495, 3019, 553, 3019, 382, 5338, 11, 28693, 8471, 448, 400, 16]}
